{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567699298,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODQzOTIzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3652#issuecomment-528439237"},"message":"See #3353 for the PR that added this.\n\nThe idea with that `--cfg-proc` exposes all procedures that start with `cfg_`, so we can express things more succinctly letting it be referred to by the last bit.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1567699305,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODQzOTI5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3652#issuecomment-528439290"},"message":"The connection is that `create -c` will only accept `cfg_*` procedures which, by pure convention, must not require any arguments to run. This was done to not complicate the `create` API too much. In general, procedures can have any number of (required) arguments.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1567699527,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODQ0MDgxNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3652#issuecomment-528440815"},"message":"thanks for the insights!","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1567699528,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjYxMTI4NjcxNw=="},"status":2}]}